            "review_title": "Review at Om Vegan Garden",
            "review_text": "Tanja T\nAlkmaar, The Netherlands25 contributions\n0\nLovely garden and food\nJul 2018 • Friends\nSuch a lovely place to enjoy lunch surrounded by nature. Plants, grass, trees, flowers, butterflies: it's an oasis in Hanoi. \n\nWe ordered the banana salad and bun nam (noodle soup), which were both absolutely delicious and very filling. The total came down to 204k for two people, which is a good deal!\n\nGo here if you love:\n- yummy food\n- friendly service\n- to be surrounded by nature\n\nSome things to keep in mind:\n- this place doesn't serve coffee. They have drinks and tea, but no coffee, I missed that. \n- It's lovely to sit outside, inside didn't look as appealing to me, it's not a cozy place to sit with friends. \n- If you sit outside to enjoy some nature, bring your mosquito spray! I left with about 16 mosquito bites. \n- Tax or service fee isn't included in the price and is 15%, that's probably mentioned somewhere but we missed it. I like it better when places just state the total price on the menu.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten July 28, 2018",
